  'event.wc2026.fact.Brazil.0': 'Five-time world champions, the most successful nation in tournament history. Pedigree everywhere.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Brazil.1': 'Last won it in 2002. Star-laden front line, technical, rhythm-based — don\'t let them settle.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Brazil.2': 'Eliminated in the quarter-finals last time out. They\'ll come hungry.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Argentina.0': 'Reigning world champions — won it in 2022. Three titles in total (1978, 1986, 2022).',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Argentina.1': 'Built around a generational core. Press them high and force errors before they get on the ball.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Argentina.2': 'They lost their opener last time and still won the lot. They thrive when written off.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.France.0': 'Won it in 1998 and 2018, finalists in 2022. The team to beat over the last decade.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.France.1': 'Pace, power, and quality off the bench. Their squad depth is the deepest in world football.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.France.2': 'Quarter-finalists or better in five of the last seven International Cups.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Germany.0': 'Four-time world champions, last won 2014. A team rebuilding from two group-stage exits.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Germany.1': 'Historically the most consistent nation at the International Cup. Always credible.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Germany.2': 'Press-resistant midfield, set-piece threat. Don\'t let crosses come in.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Spain.0': 'Won it in 2010 — their only title. Tiki-taka possession game still their identity.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Spain.1': 'They\'ll dominate the ball. Stay compact, deny the through-pass, hit them on the break.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Spain.2': 'Reigning European champions. Confidence high, midfield generation among the best.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.England.0': 'One International Cup, way back in 1966. Semi-finalists 2018, quarters 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.England.1': 'Strong on set pieces, dangerous wingers, but historically nervy in knockouts.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.England.2': 'A long-suffering nation desperate to end the wait. The pressure is on them, not us.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Uruguay.0': 'Two-time champions (1930, 1950). Small country, huge football culture.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Uruguay.1': 'Tactically disciplined, physical, never give up a goal cheaply. Famous for grit.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Uruguay.2': 'Last semi-final appearance was 2010. Rebuilding around a new generation.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Portugal.0': 'Best finish: third in 1966. Strong technical sides every cycle, rarely break through.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Portugal.1': 'A possession-based game, comfortable on the ball. Defensively suspect at times.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Portugal.2': 'Reigning Nations League champions. The talent is there, the ceiling has never been reached.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Netherlands.0': 'Three-time runners-up (1974, 1978, 2010), never won it. The great unfulfilled side.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Netherlands.1': 'Total Football heritage — fluid positional play, technical from back to front.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Netherlands.2': 'Quarter-finalists in 2022. They go deep more often than not.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Belgium.0': 'Best finish: third in 2018. Their golden generation aged out without a final.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Belgium.1': 'Clinical attacking trio, organised at the back. Capable of beating anyone on their day.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Belgium.2': 'Group-stage exit in 2022 was a shock. They\'re rebuilding around younger names.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Croatia.0': 'Runners-up 2018, third 2022. Punching above their weight with a small population.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Croatia.1': 'World-class midfield — they own the ball and tire you out. 90 minutes is rarely enough.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Croatia.2': 'Mentality monsters. Three penalty shootouts won in their last two International Cups.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Switzerland.0': 'Best finish: quarter-finals (1934, 1938, 1954). Compact, defensively solid.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Switzerland.1': 'They knocked France out on penalties at Euro 2020. Don\'t underestimate them.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Switzerland.2': 'Limited star quality but a coherent unit. They make life difficult for everyone.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Bosnia and Herzegovina.0': 'First International Cup was 2014 — beat Iran but went out in the group. Back a decade later.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Bosnia and Herzegovina.1': 'Technical, attack-minded side. Dangerous in possession, can be exposed on the counter.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Bosnia and Herzegovina.2': 'Football-mad nation making history again. Expect intensity from the first whistle.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Sweden.0': 'Best finish: runners-up 1958, third 1994. Quietly one of Europe\'s most consistent International Cup nations.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Sweden.1': 'Disciplined, physical, dangerous at set pieces. Best results come when they\'re underestimated.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Sweden.2': 'Without their iconic talisman for the first time in years. A new generation steps up.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Austria.0': 'Best finish: third in 1954. Mostly absent at the International Cup since the 1990s.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Austria.1': 'High-press, high-energy team under their current manager. Beware the opening 20 minutes.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Austria.2': 'Rarely qualifies. They\'ll see this as their tournament — expect emotion.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Norway.0': 'Best finish: round of 16, 1998. Back at a International Cup after a long absence.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Norway.1': 'Built around one of the world\'s most lethal strikers. Defend the box and you have a chance.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Norway.2': 'New generation of talent. They\'re here on merit, not a fluke.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Türkiye.0': 'Third place in 2002 — their best ever finish. Hasn\'t been back to a International Cup since 2002.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Türkiye.1': 'Passionate, physical side. Their crowd travels — atmosphere is part of their game.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Türkiye.2': 'Quality in the final third, suspect at the back. Get at them.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Czechia.0': 'As Czechoslovakia, runners-up 1934 and 1962. As Czechia, best is round of 16 in 2006.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Czechia.1': 'Tall, physical, dangerous from set pieces. Defend the second ball.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Czechia.2': 'Workmanlike rather than flashy. They will stay in matches whatever the score.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Scotland.0': 'Eight International Cup appearances, never out of the group. They make the party either way.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Scotland.1': 'Hard-working, set-piece-strong, well-organised. They\'ll run for 90 minutes.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Scotland.2': 'Their fans are louder than most stadiums. Block out the noise and impose ourselves.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Morocco.0': 'Fourth in 2022 — first African and Arab nation to reach a International Cup semi-final.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Morocco.1': 'Defensively brilliant, fast in transition. They beat Spain and Portugal on the way to the semis.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Morocco.2': 'Best African side currently. Punching well above their FIFA rank.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Senegal.0': 'African champions 2021. Round of 16 in 2002 and 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Senegal.1': 'Physical, athletic, dangerous on the break. Tighten up at the back when they break.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Senegal.2': 'Quality through the spine. They beat hosts Qatar and Ecuador to advance last time.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Tunisia.0': 'Six International Cup appearances, never past the group stage.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Tunisia.1': 'Defensively organised, disciplined, hard to break down. We\'ll need patience.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Tunisia.2': 'Famous 1-0 over France in 2022. They can pull a result out of nowhere.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Algeria.0': 'Best finish: round of 16, 2014. Eliminated by Germany in extra time.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Algeria.1': 'Talented attackers, energetic press. Don\'t give them transitions.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Algeria.2': 'Hasn\'t been to a International Cup since 2014. Ravenous to make a mark.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Egypt.0': 'Three International Cup appearances total — 1934, 1990, 2018. Never out of the group.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Egypt.1': 'Built around one talisman up front. Shut that down and the team goes with it.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Egypt.2': 'Africa Cup of Nations regulars but always seem to underperform at International Cups.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Côte d\'Ivoire.0': 'Best finish: group stage. Their golden generation flopped at three International Cups.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Côte d\'Ivoire.1': 'Physical, athletic, individually brilliant. As a team — sometimes lacking shape.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Côte d\'Ivoire.2': 'Reigning African champions. Confidence on side.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.DR Congo.0': 'Last International Cup appearance: 1974 (as Zaire). Long road back.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.DR Congo.1': 'Athletic, physical, lots of European-based talent. Tactically variable.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.DR Congo.2': 'Africa Cup of Nations semi-finalists 2024. Real signs of progress.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Cape Verde.0': 'First ever International Cup appearance. Africa Cup of Nations quarter-finalists in 2021 and 2023.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Cape Verde.1': 'Athletic, organised, believed in the upset to get here. They won\'t be starstruck.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Cape Verde.2': 'Small island nation of half a million people making history. The whole country is watching.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.South Africa.0': 'Hosted the 2010 International Cup — memorable group run with Tshabalala\'s opener still iconic.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.South Africa.1': 'African Cup of Nations champions 1996. Physical defence, fast on the counter.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.South Africa.2': '"Bafana Bafana" — the Boys. Back after 16 years away. Respect the moment.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Ghana.0': 'Two-time quarter-finalists — 2010 (lost to Uruguay on penalties), 2022 nearly.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Ghana.1': 'Pace and skill out wide. Set-piece vulnerable. Attack the back post.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Ghana.2': 'They\'ve never beaten Uruguay competitively. Long memories on both sides.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Qatar.0': '2022 International Cup hosts — became the first host nation ever to exit in the group stage.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Qatar.1': 'Asian Cup champions 2019. Have invested heavily in football infrastructure and coaching.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Qatar.2': 'Playing a International Cup without home advantage for the first time. A very different test.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Japan.0': 'Best finish: round of 16 (2002, 2010, 2018, 2022). Beat Germany and Spain in 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Japan.1': 'Disciplined, technical, well-organised. Press is excellent — sloppy passes get punished.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Japan.2': 'On the rise. Big improvement curve since 2010.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.South Korea.0': 'Fourth in 2002 (co-hosts). Round of 16 in 2010 and 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.South Korea.1': 'Tactically disciplined, athletic, dangerous on the break. World-class winger out wide.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.South Korea.2': 'They beat Portugal 2-1 in 2022 to advance. Capable of upsets.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Iran.0': 'Six International Cup appearances, never past the group stage.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Iran.1': 'Defensively organised, physical, set-piece strong. Won\'t open up.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Iran.2': 'Highest FIFA rank in Asia for years. Game management is their main flaw.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Australia.0': 'Best finish: round of 16 (2006, 2022). Tough, disciplined, physically strong.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Australia.1': 'They beat Denmark and Tunisia in 2022 to advance. Punch above their weight.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Australia.2': 'Long-ball threat, set-piece danger. Don\'t lose the second ball.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Saudi Arabia.0': 'Best finish: round of 16 in 1994. Famously beat Argentina 2-1 in 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Saudi Arabia.1': 'Compact mid-block, dangerous in transition. Their Argentina win was no fluke.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Saudi Arabia.2': 'Improved markedly under their current manager. Treat them with respect.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Uzbekistan.0': 'First-ever International Cup appearance. The Central Asian story of the cycle.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Uzbekistan.1': 'Strong qualifying campaign, tactically disciplined. The whole nation is watching.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Uzbekistan.2': 'Limited big-tournament experience but high on belief.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Jordan.0': 'First International Cup appearance ever. Asian Cup runners-up 2024 was the breakthrough.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Jordan.1': 'Counter-attacking outfit, dangerous on the break. Pacy forwards.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Jordan.2': 'No expectations on them — that makes them dangerous.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Iraq.0': 'Best finish: fourth in 1986 — their only previous International Cup. Long road back.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Iraq.1': 'Asian Cup champions 2007, the famous "year of unity" win.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Iraq.2': 'Limited resources, big heart. Treat them as anyone else, never overlook them.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.USA.0': 'Best finish: third in 1930 (only 13 teams entered). Round of 16 in 1994, 2002, 2014, 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.USA.1': 'Co-hosts in 2026 — energy, crowd, momentum all behind them.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.USA.2': 'Talent in Europe, identity still evolving. Capable of surprising the favourites.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Canada.0': 'Two International Cup appearances total (1986, 2022). No goals scored in 1986, three in 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Canada.1': 'Co-hosts in 2026. Pace out wide is genuine, defensive cohesion is the question.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Canada.2': 'Played their first ever knockout-stage tournament games at this International Cup.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Mexico.0': 'Co-hosts. Round of 16 in seven of the last eight International Cups — they always make it, never go further.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Mexico.1': '"Quinto Partido" — the fifth game (the quarter-final) is the holy grail they never reach.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Mexico.2': 'Home advantage at last. The Azteca crowd is among the most intense in football.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Panama.0': 'Second-ever International Cup appearance (first was 2018, group stage exit).',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Panama.1': 'Defensively-minded, physical at the back. Set pieces both ways.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Panama.2': 'A nation of four million — small but dangerous.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Curaçao.0': 'First International Cup appearance for the small Caribbean island of 150,000 people.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Curaçao.1': 'Regular Concacaf contenders since 2017, backed by a pool of Dutch-born talent.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Curaçao.2': 'Heavy underdogs — but Caribbean football has a long history of punching above its weight.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Haiti.0': 'First International Cup since 1974. Famously held Italy to a 1-1 draw before going out.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Haiti.1': 'Physical, direct, dangerous from set pieces. Don\'t let them settle early.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Haiti.2': 'The comeback story of this entire cycle. 52 years — and they\'re back.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Colombia.0': 'Quarter-finalists in 2014. Always-stylish South American side.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Colombia.1': 'Technical midfield, dangerous wingers. Defensively suspect at times.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Colombia.2': 'Copa América runners-up 2024. Form is on side.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Ecuador.0': 'Best finish: round of 16, 2006. Difficult to play in qualifying because of altitude.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Ecuador.1': 'Compact, athletic, well-coached. Beat Qatar and drew with Netherlands in 2022.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Ecuador.2': 'Young squad, big talent emerging. Future is bright.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Paraguay.0': 'Quarter-finalists in 2010 — drew Spain 0-0, lost 1-0. So close.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Paraguay.1': 'Defensively-organised, physical, low-block specialists. Patience is everything.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.Paraguay.2': 'They never roll over. Even when behind, the next 20 minutes will be a battle.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.New Zealand.0': 'Best finish: undefeated group exit at 2010 (drew all three).',
  'event.wc2026.fact.New Zealand.1': 'Physical, set-piece dangerous, low quality on the ball. Stay calm and play through them.',
  'event.wc2026.fact.New Zealand.2': 'OFC champions repeatedly. The big stage is the leap they keep failing to make.',
